WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Light crosses empty
space, with no charges,

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.080
no currents, and nothing to carry it.

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.390
And every frequency
travels at the same speed.

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.630
Combine two constants from
electricity and magnetism,

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.800
and out comes a speed: the
measured speed of light.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:20.740
So with nothing to carry it,
what keeps the wave going?

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.670
In this mission, you'll meet
the four equations that,

8
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.940
with the force on a charge,
fully describe electromagnetism.

9
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.690
Then you'll see why magnetic field
lines never simply begin or end.

10
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.560
Your mission: explain what keeps a
light wave going across empty space.
